cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qsim-sdk: Python client for the Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21836619
message: "If you use this software or its certification protocols in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZKSF.org (Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry)"
    email: info@zksf.org
    website: "https://zksf.org"
  - name: "Digital Venture Labs LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/official-dvl/zksf"
url: "https://zksf.org"
abstract: >-
  Python client for a cloud service that executes quantum circuits on classical
  simulators, GPU accelerators, or real quantum processors, and attaches a
  documented accuracy statement to every approximate result. Four certification
  protocols are defined: ZCC-v0.1 for simulated results, ZHF-v0.1 for
  quantum-hardware fidelity, ZQEC-v0.1 for the logical error rate of a quantum
  error correction memory experiment, reported with a 95% confidence interval,
  and ZCC-Estimate-v0.2 for error-mitigated values, stated with a statistical
  uncertainty rather than a bound, and neural ground-state energies.
  Certificates are independently verifiable without authentication.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - tensor networks
  - matrix product states
  - error bounds
  - certification
  - quantum error correction
  - surface code
  - logical qubits
  - error mitigation
license: MIT
version: 0.13.4
